The Lighthouse is an ancient artifact that crosses the space between the worlds. It is a lighthouse in shape, with a beacon that shines from a giant resonance crystal hung above its top landing, and its bare inside is older and plainer than its power suggests: concrete floors, stone walls, a single spiral staircase, creaky wooden boards, and a hand-built table with chairs. Five doors on the back wall, numbered 101 to 105, open onto other parts of it.

It was built long ago by the people of [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]], working with the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]] and the great ship Shoa, to capture the Dark Bramble. The Dark Bramble came, there was a great fight, and everyone died; the world was remade with its memory taken, and the Lighthouse stayed. It was made to quarantine power, and it does what it was built to do without asking why.

It travels. Its central body leaves one place and comes to rest in another, firing an anchor ahead of it that cracks open a [[Phenomena/Crystal Sphere|crystal sphere]] so it can descend through the break to the world inside, while its reach stays behind and the anchorways that lead to it keep working. It goes where it will, usually toward a greater concentration of a [[Divinity/Higher Kind|higher kind]].

It held [[Divinity/Immix|Immix]]'s talk show, and once Immix gave its divinity away it left the Lighthouse empty.

It was moored at the top of the City of Yellow on [[Geography/Althane/Realms/Ilkyne|Ilkyne]], and there [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] took refuge from the fall of [[Geography/Althane/The Thirteenth Realm|the Thirteenth Realm]]'s moon. It then left [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]], broke open a new crystal sphere, and came down in a forest on a world whose magic runs in six blended sources. Its reach remains behind on Althane, and it will carry passengers back by the anchorways.

The Lighthouse keeps a janitor: an old blue-skinned [[Bestiary/Realmtouched#Duskwalker|duskwalker]] in a blue boiler suit who props himself up on his mop and keeps a keychain on his belt, and who goes on when the Lighthouse goes on. He says he is happier to be heard than to be seen, that he is not technically a mister, and that he has been there as long as he has been needed. He gave [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] the keys to escape a sound stage the last time the Weft passed through the Lighthouse.
